WEBVTT

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.770
The world is in the Gourmet Age.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.370
Gourmet Hunters are explorers

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.940
who travel the world, searching 
for your ingredients.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.810
And the ingredient at 
the top of this world

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.380
is GOD, which is being sought

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.850
by one Gourmet Hunter.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.190
Go! Shock!! Gourmet!! Gourmet!!

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.700
Go! Shock!!

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.270
Friends who can eat the same dream

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.070
Friends who share the same future

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.820
With you guys

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.790
It’s first-rate gourmet my way!

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.770
If we join forces

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.530
We’ll be invincible

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.850
Come on, let’s show ‘em

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:23.460
Delicious food gives life

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:29.100
So be thankful for everything and

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.070
Let’s eat!!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.070
We can’t lose!! We 
can’t be stopped!!

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.080
We ain’t gonna let ‘em have that

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.450
We’re gonna win it!! Shock! 
Shock! Gourmet king!!

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.320
Spiked Punch!! Infinity!!

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.050
I’ll punch through with this fist

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.960
First-rate gourmet my way!

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.130
Let’s gather ‘round the table

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.030
For the sake of tomorrow

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.280
Let’s go! Go! Gourmet!!

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.070
The Cooking Fest!

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.010
The first round's event, Triathlon 
Cooking, has come to a close.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.080
Komatsu is about to start cooking 
with the ingredients he got.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.890
However, the knife he has

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.820
isn't his usual Melk Knife!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.360
Live or Die? Death in 
the Balance Cooking!!

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:44.080
That's a regular old knife.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.380
Pardon?!

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.410
What happened to the fine blade 
forged by Melk the Second?!

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.820
Chef Komatsu... Why...?

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.380
Hey, Komatsu! What's 
the matter with you?!

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.560
What the hell is that knife?!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.990
I had one of the staff here prepare it.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.810
You had one of the staff 
here prepare it...

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.630
I'm askin' what the hell happened 
to your Melk Knife, Komatsu!

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.770
My Melk Knife...

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.500
I didn't bring it from the 
cooking utensils station.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:13.940
What'd you say?!

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.670
You didn't bring it?! Why the hell not?!

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.180
After all, I came in first

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.750
and was able to get to the 
cooking utensils station in time

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.080
thanks to you, Brunch-san.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.300
I couldn't bring my Melk Knife 
back here under my own power.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:31.760
So...

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.630
...I didn't bring it back!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.330
What are you, an idiot?!

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.640
Listen here!

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.240
I dragged you along 
with me without askin'!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.370
So why would you even care 
about "your own power"?!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.270
All you should be thinkin' 
about is winning, no?!

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.710
But...

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:56.850
I want to compete!

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.550
I don't know if I can win or not...

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.220
...but I want to compete 
fair and square!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.290
Sheesh.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.350
You're a pain in the ass.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.260
Do what ya want!

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.110
You really are a dope!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.340
You put the "dumb" in dumbass...

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.340
But he's an interesting guy.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.750
Jeez...

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.520
That is just like Komatsu-kun.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.390
Kid...

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.730
He made that cocky tengu 
bastard adapt to him.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.390
You could even say it was

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.930
Komatsu's personality 
that motivated Brunch.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.250
For some reason, you can't help 
but root for Chef Komatsu.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.340
Alright, G7 is ready to judge the food!

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.540
Well, Chef Komatsu...

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.180
You chose not to use your 
own cooking utensil,

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.520
but I'm going to judge 
you no less strictly.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.220
Right!

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.460
O-Oh, no... Again...

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.300
I-I'm totally...

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.170
T-Totally nervous...

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:24.400
What should I do?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.240
Everyone is... All of 
these first-rate people...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.940
...are watching me!

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.010
His heart's beatin' fast again.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.240
The kid's heart sounds like 
it'll burst out of nervousness.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.250
Come on, Komatsu...

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.460
At this rate, he won't even be 
able to slice the ingredients.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.260
It has nothing to do with whether 
he's got his own knife or not.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.410
Alright! Let's cook!

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:01.010
Chef Komatsu brought 
many, many ingredients

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.770
from Rice Beach,

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:06.080
but they're the leftovers that 
the other chefs didn't touch.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:07.980
So, what is he going to do?

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.300
How is he going to do it?
 How is he going to cook them?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.550
Show us, Chef Komatsu!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.250
That's right...

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.890
All of you wanted to come here, right?

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.860
You wanted to participate 
with me, right?

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.220
That guy...

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.800
After mulling it over, 
what did he choose?!

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.140
Hard Crab...

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.970
Its shell is diamond-hard.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:41.450
Cooking it with that knife is 
a virtually impossible task.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.200
What?!

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.620
The knife slid right through it!

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.920
The point to insert the blade...

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.860
If he can just hold the knife 
firmly, it'll be easy to prepare.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.700
Did he hear the voice of the ingredient?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.340
That's not the only 
thing that's impressive.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.970
Even though he was a nervous 
wreck up to a few minutes ago,

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.220
he's having fun cooking!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:10.410
It's like he can't wait to bring 
out the flavor of the ingredients.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.680
Look at that face!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.580
That's Koma-chan all over!

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.320
His cooking skill has improved 
by leaps and bounds,

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:20.020
but the way he's enjoying 
himself while cooking

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.120
is classic Koma-chan!

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.320
Koma-chan, you can do it!

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.420
Finished!

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.040
What?! Only the Hard Crab?!

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.840
What a simple dish...

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:50.560
Please try pushing on the shell 
lightly with the tip of a spoon.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.420
What?!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.920
The Hard Crab's shell is as 
crispy as a potato chip?!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.660
If you boil it for nine 
minutes and 6.2 seconds

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.300
in oil at the low temperature 
of 96.2 degrees,

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.890
the hard shell becomes crispy 
and deliciously edible.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.000
I knew that.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.470
But preparing that oil 
is extremely difficult.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.780
I suppose it shows just 
how talented he is.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.610
This is...

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.680
I call it "Beach Fried Rice".

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.990
Fried rice is inside of the crab!

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:31.760
It looks delicious!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:35.240
Alright, G7, the taste test, please!

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.360
Please try it.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.550
Thank you for the food.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.800
I'm feeling it even from the spoon.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.230
The refreshing texture of the rice...

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.710
The scent of the sea is quite pleasant.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:00.390
This is the rice from Rice 
Beach, the very dunes

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.920
where all the ingredients were laid.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.320
Right!

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.660
Was I not allowed to use it?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.500
No, it's no problem at all.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.670
But to use that most common of rice...

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.080
Right...

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.840
It seemed like a waste not to...

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.250
A waste?

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:20.200
Yes.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:27.310
You brought out the flavors 
of many, many ingredients

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.080
and used ingredients that the 
other chefs didn't touch.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.680
In a word, "leftovers"...

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.790
I thought maybe the best way

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.770
to make use of all the

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:39.490
ingredients I brought 
back was with fried rice.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.910
It certainly is a fun 
and delicious dish.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.730
Thank you!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.970
Komatsu really is an 
interesting character.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:50.500
He can't lose.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.800
Alright, next up

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.530
is me.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.110
The Cooking Festival,

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:00.310
where World Ranked chefs 
show off their skills!

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:05.680
Alright! Who will be the chefs to clear

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.470
this first round, Triathlon Cooking?

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.820
Who?!

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:13.750
Alright, cooking time is up!

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:18.750
And now I'll announce 
our successful chefs!

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.900
First, the living National 
Treasures, Setsuno

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.530
and Zaus!

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.000
Yuda! Brunch!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.610
Livebearer! Chiru!

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:31.540
Wabutora! And...

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.070
...Chef Komatsu!

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.180
I did it!

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.780
I made it past the first round!

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.420
Did you hear that, everyone?!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.140
We heard.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.320
Who gets that happy about 
passing the first round?

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.540
He's excited.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.130
He's definitely excited.

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:51.000
You'd think he won the whole shebang.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.000
Yeesh. That's pretty cocky...

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:02.210
We have our 50 remaining chefs!

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.220
And now let's go on to the second round.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.750
The second round is...

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.230
...this!

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.000
W-What the hell is that?!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:45.220
For this first match of Death in 
the Balance Cooking, as decided

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:48.270
by fortune cookies, 
here's our first player!

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:51.160
Hotel Gourmet's Chef Komatsu!

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:54.160
And competing against 
him is the Oil Artisan,

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.390
Chef Wabutora!

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.930
Okay, and now I'll explain the rules.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:03.990
Each side has the same amount 
of ingredients on their scale.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.640
The idea is for them to 
quickly cook the ingredients,

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.640
which will be eaten by 
some of our spectators.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:12.480
If the amount of ingredients decrease,

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.350
that side of the scale will rise,

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.750
while the opponent's scale will lower.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.820
And waiting below them is a 
cauldron of roiling flames!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.520
It's a competition in which 
cooking speed is key!

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:27.550
Chef Komatsu, I'm going to use 
the Mors Oil that you discovered.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:29.330
So I want you to use

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:33.900
your Melk Knife and come at 
me with everything you've got!

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.100
Alright, the first match...

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.770
Start!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.940
My opponent is the Oil 
Artisan, Chef Wabutora.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.850
Anyway, I'll give it my best shot!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.940
But how...?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.220
I'm not only using Mors Oil!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:53.220
Second Oil and Simmer Oil!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.120
High temperature heat 
is achieved in moments!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.990
Which gives me oil that can 
deep-fry ingredients fast!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.530
Secret technique! Oil Offensive!

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.700
For this match, Chef Wabutora is 
cooking up his deep-fried food!

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:16.190
A special sampling of 
Wabutora's wares is done!

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:17.780
That was fast!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:21.980
Uh-oh! Chef Komatsu's 
plate is going down!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.620
Koma-chan!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.490
Hot...

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.160
I'll be cooked myself in 
a matter of moments...

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:35.830
That's it!

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:39.640
What's this?!

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:42.730
Chef Komatsu has brought out 
his treasured blade at last!

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.300
His Melk Knife!

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.940
He's cut-cut-cutting 
all of the ingredients!

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:54.110
He can cut like that because 
he's mastered Honoring the Food.

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:56.080
Well done, Komatsu-kun.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.950
Wow. He's that good...

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.150
Thank you, Chef Komatsu.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:03.820
And so...

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.190
He's mixed the ingredients 
in the giant bowl.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.660
What?! What is this?!

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:13.730
Uh-oh! As Chef Komatsu is cooking, 
people are eat-eat-eating!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:15.300
This is delicious!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.230
Men and women, young and old

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.870
are eating Chef Wabutora's fried food!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.740
Even the old folks, who don't 
usually like fried food,

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:24.010
are gleefully wolfing it down!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.040
Of course it's delicious,

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.010
but he made the mince 
cutlets, deep-fried chicken,

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.980
and pork cutlets all bite-sized,

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:33.220
so they can be eaten easily.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.350
That's not all.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:38.390
Chef Wabutora is doling out 
the food a little at a time,

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.470
feeding them while stimulating 
their appetites.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.260
I see...

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.140
They say that just seeing a lot of

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:46.300
food is enough to make you full.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.200
I hate itty-bitty bite-sized pieces...

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:53.340
It shows that he's really

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:55.340
fired up with Komatsu 
as his competition.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:58.710
The cutlet's fried!

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:02.250
The cutlets keep coming 
up and so does his scale!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.150
Chef Komatsu is going down!

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:07.290
Chef Komatsu is in a pinch as he 
gets even closer to the flames!

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.890
A big pinch!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.690
It'll work! As long 
as I have this heat...

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.500
It's oil!

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.500
Now he's lifting up the ingredients...

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:24.440
Oh, boy! He threw it 
onto the scale's plate.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.360
Now what's this?

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.670
He keeps rolling the mixture around.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.940
And now Chef Komatsu has got

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:32.480
an ultra-big spatula!

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:50.430
Hamburger steak!

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:54.020
Giant hamburger steaks 
in a variety of shapes!

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.540
Hamburger steak?!

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.400
Has he lost his mind?!

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:01.470
What's Komatsu thinkin'?!

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.930
It'll take forever for those flames

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:04.810
to cook his hamburger steaks!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:05.480
No.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:06.970
Look carefully.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:08.550
They're already cooked.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.420
What?!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.950
The flames are reaching...

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:14.850
The meat's cooking.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:17.660
It's like the scale's plate is an oven!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.220
And he can cook in that heat?!

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:24.260
Compared to the time 
I went to Sand Garden

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.270
with Toriko-san and Zebra-san...

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.000
...this is nothing!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.710
O-Oh, my!

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:42.950
He combined them into a 
king-sized hamburger steak!

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:45.180
We're talking ultra-big size!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:48.220
A king-sized hamburger steak?!

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:50.090
You had this in mind the whole time?!

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:51.590
That's right!

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:53.120
I learned something 
at the Gourmet Casino.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.860
No matter how unfavorable 
the situation is,

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:59.460
don't give up, but think 
calmly, like Coco-san did.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:01.600
Komatsu-kun...

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.740
And now he's rolling down some cheese!

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.040
It's like a cheese festival!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:12.110
The cheese is 
rolling-rolling-rolling-rolling...

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.450
Now it jumped up and landed 
on the hamburger steak!

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:16.610
It's melting!

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:19.720
At a normal temperature, it 
would retain its hardened form,

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.390
but this heat is melting 
the cheese like butter!

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.160
It suits the hamburger steak to a T!

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:27.630
My Jumboburger is done!

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:32.990
My final fried treats are done too!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:36.570
Both of them used up 
all their ingredients.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:41.670
Which dish will the spectators 
polish off first?!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.090
This has become Sudden 
Death in the Balance!

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:45.840
But!

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:49.580
Chef Komatsu's Jumboburger 
is really popular!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.220
Even more popular than the 
food on Chef Wabutora's table?

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.790
Overwhelmingly so!

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:58.250
The oil I used to fry 
the hamburger steak...

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.930
...is the Mors Oil I captured 
with Sunny-san and Toriko-san.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.730
It's dense but silky, 
so it's not overly rich.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.170
That's why people can eat a lot of it.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:09.300
Matsu...

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:12.500
If you mix Second Oil and 
Simmer Oil with Mors Oil,

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.840
the food will cook faster,

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.720
but it becomes just a little too rich.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:21.450
So making cooking speed my priority 
by mixing the oils backfired...

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.260
Just that slight difference 
was the cause of my defeat.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:30.250
That and having something 
everybody could split

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.320
increased their appetites and 
made it taste even better!

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:36.490
That's the way I've learned 
to cook by traveling

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.180
with Toriko-san and the others.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:43.190
To think the Oil Artisan, Wabutora, 
could be schooled like this...

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.940
This part has minced sardines!

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.670
Its light flavor ties it all together.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.290
There are shrimp in this 
part! Nice and plump!

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:52.710
You're right!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.050
It seems the flavor is different,

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.650
depending on which part you eat!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.210
The Jumboburger isn't just about size,

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:01.590
its flavor is jumbo-grade too!

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:03.790
Thank you for the food!

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.360
The Jumboburger is all gone!

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:10.570
Chef Komatsu with a 
delicious comeback win!

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.420
That was brilliant, Chef Komatsu.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.140
Sunny was right about you after all.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.170
You have extraordinary cooking sense.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:26.210
If you don't win this, 
I'll never forgive you.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.690
The two shake hands. That's 
wonderful chef-ship!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:37.320
I'm moved to tears!

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:41.460
A great deal of oil is seeping 
out of Wabutora's hand.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.230
That's sweat.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.770
It's delicious when 
everyone eats together...

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.470
That's very Komatsu.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.170
Well, he did a good job.

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:54.970
That was awesome, Komatsu!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.880
Don't get cocky just 'cause you won!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.110
This is becoming a serious 
competition with him.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:05.020
But first I gotta put an 
end to these oldsters.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:10.320
I warn you, these oldsters 
are really strong.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:11.120
Setsu-san...

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:14.960
We can't afford to just stand 
around and do nothing either.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:32.390
Tomorrow’s wind is gonna blow tomorrow

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:39.720
So your adventurous life 
will be sensational

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:45.240
Only a smile has no flavor, 
so wipe your tears

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:51.830
After a downpour of rain from the 
sky, the sun always rises high

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:57.670
Every time I know you’re 
working up a sweat

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:03.040
My heart races and I become captivated

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.880
Don’t give up!

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:12.100
I’m closest to you in 
the middle of a challenge

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:16.670
Always believe in yourself!

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:29.530
Guess the Legend
The Legend Gourmet Quiz

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:27.570
Guess the Legend!

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:29.530
The Legend Gourmet Quiz!

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.320
I'm your host, Tina.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.900
In this segment, you 
guess the legendary

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:35.900
ingredients of the Gourmet Age!

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.710
Really?! Level 6

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.710
Today's "Really?!" level is 6.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.620
Heavenly voice! Please 
help me today too!

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.820
Someone once said...

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:52.720
There's something that lives 
in the scorching desert

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:57.900
that's got a hump made 
out of piping hot gratin.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:00.260
The allotted time limit is 10 seconds.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:01.630
Start!

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.640
Gratin? Hump? It's a camel!

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.640
There you go.

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:08.340
Camel and gratin... Grameltin?

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:09.340
Close!

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.610
Cametin? Tincamel?

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:14.910
Someone once said...

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:18.620
There's something that lives 
in the scorching desert

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:26.560
Camegratin

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:21.450
that's got a hump made 
out of piping hot gratin.

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:24.880
Camegratin!

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:29.190
I don't think that's any 
better than my guesses...

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:31.230
Complainer!

00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:33.030
Maybe I won't come back next time.

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:34.930
Oh, no, I was just kidding!

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:36.040
Thank you for the delicious

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:38.440
riddle that was very easy to understand!

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:39.870
Please come back next time!

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:41.870
Well, I'll think about it.

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:43.980
And now, our next segment!
